.TH DOTFILES-SYNC 1 "2026-10-25" "dotfiles-sync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotfiles-sync \- push and pull dotfiles, configs, scripts, and packages via Git
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotfiles-sync.sh setup
.P
.B dotfiles-sync.sh push
[\fIcommit-message\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.P
.B dotfiles-sync.sh pull
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-skip\-cachyos\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dotfiles-sync.sh
mirrors your configuration between machines through a Git repository.
It handles dotfiles (symlinked), copy-only configs (e.g. Electron apps),
custom scripts from
.IR ~/.local/bin ,
man pages,
and package lists split by source (Arch official, CachyOS, and AUR).
.P
The script is designed to set up a new Arch-based system in one command.
On pull it auto-detects whether the CachyOS repositories are available
and adds them if missing, then installs every package one at a time,
logging failures for review instead of silently dropping them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would happen without changing anything on disk.
Also skips Git commit/push on
.BR push .
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-cachyos
(Only meaningful for
.BR pull .)
Do not attempt to add the CachyOS repositories.
Packages in
.I pkglist-cachyos.txt
are skipped and logged to
.IR skipped-cachyos.txt .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Clone the dotfiles repository from GitHub into
.IR ~/dotfiles
and create the expected directory layout
.RI ( dotfiles/ ", " configs/kde/ ", " scripts/ ", " packages/ ).
Safe to run more than once \(en exits early if the repo already exists.
.TP
.B push " [\fImsg\fR]"
Save the current system state to the repo and push it to GitHub.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Dumps package lists:
.B pkglist-arch.txt
(Arch official),
.B pkglist-cachyos.txt
(CachyOS repo),
.B pkglist-aur.txt
(AUR/foreign).
.IP \(bu 2
Syncs
.B ~/.local/bin
into
.I scripts/
with
.B rsync \-\-delete
so the mirror is pruned to match exactly. Backup and cache files are
excluded, and
.B \-\-delete\-excluded
also removes any that were mirrored previously (see
.BR FILES ).
.IP \(bu 2
Syncs symlink targets (e.g.
.BR ~/.config/fish )
into
.I dotfiles/
with
.B rsync
\fB\-\-delete\fR.
Some noisy subdirectories are excluded (see
.BR FILES ).
.IP \(bu 2
Copies copy-only configs (Electron apps, KDE, systemd user units,
autostart entries, desktop launchers, theming, audio) into
.IR configs/ ,
and the single-file home dotfiles
.RB ( .gitconfig ", " .bashrc ", " .zshrc ", " .gtkrc\-2.0 )
into
.IR dotfiles/home/ .
.IP \(bu 2
Commits with the supplied message (default:
"chore: sync dotfiles YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM"), then runs
.B git pull \-\-rebase
before pushing, so a commit made on another machine can never leave the
sync half-applied. An unmergeable divergence aborts with an error instead
of pushing.
.RE
.TP
.B pull " [\fIflags\fR]"
Restore everything from the repo onto the current machine.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Runs
.B git pull
in
.IR ~/dotfiles .
.IP \(bu 2
If on Arch Linux and CachyOS repos are absent, downloads and installs
.B cachyos-keyring
and
.BR cachyos-mirrorlist ,
appends
.B [cachyos]
to
.IR /etc/pacman.conf ,
and refreshes the database.
.IP \(bu 2
Installs each package list one-by-one:
.B pkglist-arch.txt
and
.B pkglist-cachyos.txt
with
.BR pacman ,
.B pkglist-aur.txt
with
.BR paru .
Failures are written to
.IR failed.txt .
.IP \(bu 2
Hardware-specific packages (GPU drivers, microcode, vendor kernels)
are skipped automatically and logged to
.IR skipped-hardware.txt .
.IP \(bu 2
Restores scripts to
.I ~/.local/bin
with
.BR "rsync \-\-delete" ,
so a script deleted from the repo is also removed from the live directory.
Scripts are made executable with
.BR find
on regular files only. Excluded paths
.RB ( VR*CyberDeck* ", " *.AppImage )
are shielded from deletion, so the portable app survives a pull.
.IP \(bu 2
Creates symlinks for all dotfile targets, backing up any existing
real file or directory to a timestamped
.IB name .bak.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS .
.IP \(bu 2
Copies copy-only configs back to their original locations (same backup
behaviour as symlinks), merging directory contents rather than nesting them.
.IP \(bu 2
Runs
.B mandb \-u ~/.local/share/man
to index restored man pages.
.RE
.SH HARDWARE EXCLUSIONS
To avoid installing GPU drivers and CPU microcode meant for a different
machine, the following package names are skipped on
.BR pull :
.IP \(bu 2
AMD GPU:
.BR vulkan-radeon ", " lib32-vulkan-radeon ", " amdvlk ", " lib32-amdvlk ", "
.BR xv86-video-amdgpu ", " radeontop ", " rocm-opencl-runtime ", "
.BR rocm-hip-runtime ", " libva-mesa-driver ", " lib32-libva-mesa-driver ", "
.BR mesa-vdpau ", " lib32-mesa-vdpau ", " rocm-core ", " rocm-smi-lib ", "
.BR hip-runtime-amd ", " composable-kernel
.IP \(bu 2
AMD CPU:
.B amd-ucode
.IP \(bu 2
NVIDIA:
.BR nvidia-dkms ", " nvidia-utils ", " lib32-nvidia-utils ", "
.BR libva-nvidia-driver ", " nvidia-prime ", " nvidia-settings ", " nvtop
.IP \(bu 2
Intel GPU:
.BR vulkan-intel ", " intel-media-driver ", " libva-intel-driver ", "
.B intel-ucode
.IP \(bu 2
CachyOS kernels:
.BR linux-cachyos ", " linux-cachyos-headers ", " linux-cachyos-lts ", "
.BR linux-cachyos-lts-headers ", " linux-cachyos-nvidia
.SH ENVIRONMENT
None. Repository location
.RI ( ~/dotfiles )
and remote URL are fixed in the script; they are not read from the
environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/dotfiles/
Git working tree with the following layout:
.RS
.TP
.I dotfiles/
Symlink targets (Alacritty, btop, container/Quadlet units, fastfetch, fish,
Ghostty, Haruna, MangoHud, mpv, Neovim, qBittorrent, XnView MP, etc.)
.TP
.I dotfiles/home/
Single-file home dotfiles restored to
.IR "$HOME" :
.BR .gitconfig ", " .bashrc ", " .bash_profile ", " .bash_logout ", "
.BR .zshrc ", " .gtkrc\-2.0 .
.TP
.I configs/
Copied configs. KDE and per-app configs live in subdirectories; individual
files such as
.I dolphinrc
and
.I katerc
sit at the top.
.TP
.I configs/kde/
Individual KDE config files:
.BR kdeglobals ", " kglobalshortcutsrc ", " kwinrc ", " kwinrulesrc ", "
.BR kcminputrc ", " kscreenlockerrc ", " powerdevilrc ", "
.BR powermanagementprofilesrc ", " mimeapps.list .
.TP
.I configs/autostart/
Session autostart entries from
.IR ~/.config/autostart .
.TP
.I configs/systemd/
User units and timers from
.IR ~/.config/systemd/user ,
including
.I *.wants
enablement symlinks.
.TP
.I configs/applications/
Hand-written desktop launchers from
.IR ~/.local/share/applications .
Wine-generated entries and
.I mimeinfo.cache
are excluded.
.TP
.I configs/color-schemes/
KDE colour schemes referenced by
.IR kdeglobals .
.TP
.I configs/gtk\-3.0/ ", " configs/gtk\-4.0/
GTK theme CSS written by the KDE GTK-configurator.
.TP
.I configs/pipewire/ ", " configs/wireplumber/
PipeWire and WirePlumber drop-in configs (EQ, Bluetooth codec policy).
.TP
.I configs/micro/
micro settings and keybindings only; the 650K upstream
.I syntax/
tree is excluded.
.TP
.I configs/obsidian/
Only
.IR obsidian.json ,
the vault list. The rest of that directory is Electron state and is
no longer mirrored.
.TP
.I configs/man/
Custom man pages from
.IR ~/.local/share/man
.TP
.I scripts/
Every script and binary from
.IR ~/.local/bin ,
mirrored with
.B rsync \-\-delete
so removed scripts do not linger.
.TP
.I packages/
.IR pkglist-arch.txt ,
.IR pkglist-cachyos.txt ,
.IR pkglist-aur.txt ,
.IR failed.txt ,
.IR skipped-hardware.txt ,
.I skipped-cachyos.txt
.RE
.TP
.I Global excludes
Every
.B rsync
skips
\fB*.bak\fR,
\fB*.bak.*\fR,
\fB*.bak\-*\fR,
\fB*.asar\fR,
\fB__pycache__/\fR
and
\fB*.pyc\fR.
On the push mirror this is combined with
.B \-\-delete\-excluded
so previously mirrored copies are purged from the repository. The pull
restore deliberately omits
.B \-\-delete\-excluded
(it uses plain
.BR \-\-delete ),
which protects excluded paths on the live side.
Machine-specific runtime state such as
.I dotfiles/mpv/window-state.json
is kept out through the repository
.IR .gitignore .
.TP
.I Per-path excludes
The following paths carry their own exclude list on top of the globals:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.I dotfiles/xnviewmp
\(en
.BR Thumb.db ", " XnView.db ", " XnView\-*.db ,
SQLite sidecars. The thumbnail cache alone is several gigabytes.
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/copyparty ", " configs/kdeconnect ", " configs/jellyfin\-mpv\-shim
\(en keys, salts, session state and server credentials (see
.BR SECRETS ).
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/vesktop ", " configs/legcord ", " configs/discord ", " configs/brave
\(en Electron
.BR Cache/ ", " Code*Cache/ ", " GPUCache/ ", " Service*Worker/ ", "
.BR Local*Storage/ ", " sessionData/ ;
only settings and preferences are kept.
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/applications
\(en
.BR wine/ ", " wine\-*.desktop ", " discord\-*.desktop ", " mimeinfo.cache .
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/opencode
\(en
.BR node_modules/ ", " auth.json ,
lockfiles.
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/micro
\(en
.BR syntax/ ", " buffers/ .
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/man
\(en
.IR index.db ,
the binary
.B mandb
cache, which is rebuilt on pull.
.RE
.TP
.I ~/.config/gallery-dl/
Not synced at all: its config carries a session cookie for Pixiv.
.TP
.I Script source excludes
The scripts sync from
.I ~/.local/bin
additionally skips large portable application bundles that must never
enter the repository: the glob
.B VR*CyberDeck*
(the VR CyberDeck portable app and its
.I VRCyberDeck.ini
state file) and
.BR *.AppImage .
Because exclude patterns are word-split, they must not contain spaces.
As with the global excludes, any matching files already mirrored into
.I scripts/
are purged by
.BR \-\-delete\-excluded .
.TP
.I ~/dotfiles/packages/failed.txt
Packages that failed to install on pull (one per line).
.TP
.I ~/dotfiles/packages/skipped-hardware.txt
Hardware-specific packages skipped on pull (requires manual install).
.TP
.I ~/dotfiles/packages/skipped-cachyos.txt
CachyOS packages skipped when
.B \-\-skip\-cachyos
is used.
.TP
.I ~/.config/qBittorrent/
On push, the following are excluded and do not reach the repo:
.BR BT_backup/ ", " logs/ ", " rss/ ", " search/ ", " GeoIP/ ", "
.BR qBittorrent.conf ", " qBittorrent-data.conf .
.SH SECRETS
The repository is private but is still treated as untrusted. These are never
committed, enforced twice: by an
.B rsync
exclude and by a matching
.I .gitignore
entry.
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/copyparty/cert.pem
\(en TLS private key.
.IP \(bu 2
.IR configs/copyparty/{ah,dk,fk}\-salt.txt ", " iphash ", " sessions.db
\(en password salts and live sessions.
.IP \(bu 2
.IR configs/kdeconnect/{certificate,privateKey}.pem
\(en device identity; regenerate per machine by pairing again.
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/jellyfin\-mpv\-shim/cred.json
\(en Jellyfin server token.
.IP \(bu 2
.I configs/opencode/auth.json
\(en provider API credentials.
.IP \(bu 2
.I ~/.config/aur\-review/key
\(en reviewer API key; that path is not part of any sync list.
.IP \(bu 2
.I ~/.ssh/
\(en never synced. Keep a sanitized
.I config.example
in the repo by hand if you want the host layout backed up.
.P
Because
.I ~/.config/systemd
is synced wholesale, user units must never embed credentials in
.B Environment=
lines. Put them in
.RB ( %h/.config/supermemory/env
for example), mode 600, and reference the file with
.BR EnvironmentFile= .
That path is outside every sync list and outside the repository.
.P
Not affected by the above: the synced
.I ~/.local/share/man
tree and
.I ~/.config/opencode
skills contain documentation only, no keys.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh setup
First run on any machine. Clones the dotfiles repo.
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh push
Save current state. Equivalent to
.BR "dotfiles-sync.sh push 'chore: sync dotfiles ...'" .
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh push "add nvim config"
Save with a custom commit message.
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh push --dry-run
Preview what would be pushed without making changes.
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh pull
Full restore.
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh pull --dry-run
Preview everything that would be installed and linked.
.TP
dotfiles-sync.sh pull --skip-cachyos
Restore without touching CachyOS repositories or its packages.
.TP
cat ~/dotfiles/packages/failed.txt
Review packages that failed to install after a pull.
.TP
cat ~/dotfiles/packages/skipped-hardware.txt
See which GPU/CPU packages were skipped \(en install equivalents
for your hardware.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or nothing to commit, or dry run completed).
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (missing required command, repo not found, etc.).
Individual package install failures do
.I not
cause a non-zero exit; they are logged instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR paru (1),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR mandb (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Killian for local use on Arch-based systems.
